# Code ownership.
#
# A team is only honoured as a code owner if it has WRITE access to this repository.
# Grant it first under Settings > Collaborators and teams. A team named here without
# access is ignored silently: no error, no warning, and no review is ever requested.
# The same applies to a team that does not exist.
#
# Review scheme: ONE required reviewer. Each path names a single team, so GitHub
# requests exactly one approval. Listing two teams on a path would require an
# approval from each of them.
#
# Sensitive paths are not reviewed by more people: they are reviewed by a
# different team. See "Review scheme" in README.md.
